            <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-900">File format</th>
            <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-900">Deployment notes</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-100">
          <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-900 font-medium">Slican</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600">WAV 8 kHz mono μ-law / GSM 6.10</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600">Most popular PBX in Polish SMB - requires 8 kHz μ-law for full compatibility</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-900 font-medium">Platan</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600">WAV PCM 8 kHz / MP3 acceptable</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600">Platan Libra, Optima centrals - WAV PCM compatibility, MP3 for newer models</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-900 font-medium">Asterisk / FreePBX</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600">WAV 8 kHz/16 kHz mono</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600">Open-source VoIP - accepts WAV in many variants, most often 8 kHz mono</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-900 font-medium">3CX</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600">WAV PCM / MP3</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600">VoIP system popular with larger companies - format flexibility, MP3 for quick deploy</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-900 font-medium">Cisco UCM</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600">WAV ulaw / alaw 8 kHz</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600">Enterprise-grade - requires ulaw (US) or alaw (EU) depending on region</td></tr>
